 chow. Across has F2 pung, B3B4B5 chow. Previous has B5 pung, B6B7B8 chow. So many terminals and honors are used.  \n\nThus, discard T1.  \n\nReason: T1 has the fewest remaining copies (only 1 left) making it difficult to form a pair or meld. Keeping T2 and T4 offers better potential to complete a chow with T3 (4 left), and W4 and B4 have reasonable remaining copies for pairing. This maximizes flexibility to form the final meld and pair needed for a winning hand.  \n\nAnswer: Play T1"}
